-- title:
--   Weight-2m Hecke operator preserves the Riemann–Roch space
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$, a positive integer $N$ with $(N : K) \ne 0$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \ne p$, together with an integer $m \ge 1$. Write $F = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ K\ N$ for the $K$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ K$ generated by the series $\mathrm{jqModC}\ K$ and its substitution $q \mapsto q^N$, and $R = \mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\ K\ N\ \ell$ for the $K$-subfield generated by $\mathrm{jqModC}\ K$ and its substitutions $q \mapsto q^N$, $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$, $q \mapsto q^{N\ell}$. Let $G \in F$ satisfy the condition defining $\mathrm{riemannRochSpace}(\mathrm{weightDivisor}\ K\ N\ m)$, namely that at every place $v$ of $F$ over $K$ the adic valuation of $G$ is at most $\exp$ of the value at $v$ of the divisor $\mathrm{weightDivisor}\ K\ N\ m$ (the divisor agreeing with the floor function $\mathrm{weightFloor}\ K\ N\ m$ at every place if such a finitely supported function exists, and $0$ otherwise). Give $R$ the $F$-algebra structure along $\mathrm{heckeAlphaC}$, the inclusion $F \hookrightarrow R$. Then the element $\ell^{m-1} \cdot \mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}\bigl(\mathrm{heckeBetaC}(G)\cdot h^{m}\bigr)$ of $F$, where $\mathrm{heckeBetaC}$ is the $K$-algebra map $F \to R$ given by $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ and $h = \mathrm{heckeMultiplier}\ N\ K\ \ell$ is the element of $R$ chosen so that $d(\mathrm{heckeBetaC}(j)) = h \cdot$ (the image in $\Omega_{R/K}$ of $d j$), again satisfies the same condition, i.e. lies in $\mathrm{riemannRochSpace}(\mathrm{weightDivisor}\ K\ N\ m)$.
--
--   This is the stability of the space of holomorphic weight-$2m$ modular functions on the level-$N$ modular curve in characteristic $p$ under the Hecke correspondence at $\ell$, realised here as the trace along the $\ell$-degeneracy roof twisted by the $m$-th power of the Hecke multiplier; it is what makes $T_\ell^{(m)}$ an endomorphism of the finite-dimensional Riemann–Roch space attached to the weight divisor. It is used in the assembly of the supersingular Hecke window, [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.ssHeckeFun_window`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.ssHeckeFun_window).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_SSHeckeV2_trace_heckeBetaC_mul_pow_mem_riemannRochSpace_weightDivisor.lean

